&gt;Growing up in the 90s, television was a different experience.
&gt;
&gt;You turned on the TV, and whatever was playing at that moment would become your entertainment.
&gt;
&gt;Nowadays you yourself are in control, you choose what you want to see, whenever you want.<p>You had some control back then, too -- you could change the channel. I don&#x27;t know anywhere that had a single OTA channel in the 1990s.<p>(And &quot;Stargate SG-1&quot; was on cable.)
